  "summary": "GPU cloud selling on-demand instances by the minute, with no spot market and no contract. Its pricing page lists one hourly rate per GPU in US dollars, drawn by a script; the figure here is that rate as printed. Storage is priced separately per terabyte-hour. The page says nothing about VAT.",
  "notes": "Single-page app: the served HTML is a shell with no figure, so the page is rendered (_render, our user agent) and the \"GPU Pricing\" card is read with its defaults, USD and Per hour - one \"$N/hour\" row per GPU. H100-PCIe-80GB and H100-PCIe-NVLink-80GB are both h100-pcie (80 GB); the cheaper is the quote, the row name is the instance. per_gpu, gpu_count 1, scope instance, on_demand, region null; EUR and INR buttons not read; no word on VAT. Card names match Hyperstack flavours - not stated whether it runs on that capacity",
